@* The logo is a single-path navy SVG (Docs/PhillyPause.svg). Rendering it as a
   CSS mask rather than an <img> lets it take any colour from --logo-ink, so the
   same one file works on the bone page and on the navy ground.

   It is a square stacked lockup — bell above, wordmark below — so it needs
   room. Below about 64px the wordmark stops being legible; a horizontal
   lockup and a mark-only variant are the two files still missing. *@

<span class="logo @Class" style="--logo-size: @(Size)px" role="img" aria-label="PhillyPause"></span>

@code {
    [Parameter] public int Size { get; set; } = 72;

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
